get-test-result-needs-test: TPM2_GetTestResult reports untested functions

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, TPM2_GetTestResult): "If TPM2_SelfTest() has
not been executed and a testable function has not been tested, testResult
will be TPM_RC_NEEDS_TEST. If TPM2_SelfTest() has been received and the tests
are not complete, testResult will be TPM_RC_TESTING. If testing of all
functions is complete without functional failures, testResult will be
TPM_RC_SUCCESS."

The reference always returns TPM_RC_SUCCESS (its comment: "the behavior in
this function is NOT the correct behavior for a real TPM implementation").
Self tests run synchronously (TPM2_SelfTest() completes every test before it
returns, and an untested algorithm is tested on its first use), so testing
is never "in progress": testResult is TPM_RC_NEEDS_TEST while any algorithm
remains to be tested (a bit of g_toTest is SET, the toDoList of
TPM2_IncrementalSelfTest() is not empty) and TPM_RC_SUCCESS otherwise, as in
tpm-rs.

diff --git a/src/CryptUtil.c b/src/CryptUtil.c
--- a/src/CryptUtil.c
+++ b/src/CryptUtil.c
@@ -1705,6 +1705,15 @@ CryptGetTestResult(TPM2B_MAX_BUFFER* outData  // OUT: test result data
 		   )
 {
     outData->t.size = 0;
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // TPM_RC_NEEDS_TEST while a testable function is untested (Part 3
+    // TPM2_GetTestResult; the tests run synchronously, so never TPM_RC_TESTING).
+    {
+        UINT32 i;
+        for(i = 0; i < sizeof(g_toTest); i++)
+            if(g_toTest[i] != 0)
+                return TPM_RC_NEEDS_TEST;
+    }
     return TPM_RC_SUCCESS;
 }
 
